# aux/statusbar shows a bar for the progress of a job. It reads lines of two numbers, the part that is done and the full size, from its standard input. It makes a new window, so the script gives it the rectangle of the window under test, 724,688,1024,768. The bar shows 3 of 4, and statusbar stops when the input ends after 15 seconds.
class exact
window 300x80
run {echo 3 4; sleep 15} | aux/statusbar -w 724,688,1024,768 copy
pause 2
quiet
snap open
exit none
